      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 International Society for Neurochemistry.",
        "AbstractText": "In this editorial, we highlight the recent work of Dorninger et al. that demonstrates a reduction in plasmalogens in the motor end plate is associated with a reduction in motor end plate function. This reduction in function is illuminated in reduced muscle function in these mice, corresponding with the reduction in acetylcholine release and in its receptor density observed in these mice."
